  "title": "BOOM TOWN",
  "summary": "<em>“This is not utopia. This is a neighborhood of speculation. This is Times Square. Or that fracking town in North Dakota with the $15 Budweisers while supplies last.”</em> - Peter Burr\r\n\r\nPeter Burr’s BOOM TOWN is a fictional neighborhood on the blockchain inspired by towns that live and die with the boom and bust cycles of speculation. The landscape of the American West was at one point littered with boomtowns — make-shift settlements that sprung up wherever gold, silver, oil, or other valuable resources were to be found. Animated by the imaginaries of Manifest Destiny, colonialist expansion, and get-rich-quick schemes, boomtowns attracted prospectors, speculators, and those in search of a fast track to a better life. San Francisco was one such town, swelling from a village of 800 people to a city of 35,000 in five short years during the Gold Rush, and subsequently ballooning to over 230,000 just 20 years later thanks to a massive silver find in the nearby mountains of Lake Tahoe. But once the resources are depleted, many boomtowns fall into disuse — abandoned as quickly as they appeared. Some become ghost towns that are simply left to ruin. Others, like San Francisco, reinvent themselves and live to see another windfall. \r\n\r\nLike most of his works, Burr’s BOOM TOWN is a richly crafted narrative world that is deeply evocative while remaining mysterious and restrained. Displaying the artist’s gift for creating images and environments that hover on the boundary between abstraction and figuration, they invite the viewer to fill in the blanks with their own interpretation, suggesting a story that is barely legible yet unmistakably present. Inspired by the tools and aesthetics of video games, Burr’s compositions draw on generative dynamics and the complexity that emerges from simple, rule-based systems. Each of the eight works in BOOM TOWN follows a precise logic for generating the structure’s architecture, its ground and field, its shadows, planes, and colors. Th...",
  "coverImage": "https://imagedelivery.net/iCRs13uicXIPOWrnuHbaKA/b6edd9fd-bbe3-4f17-f228-9d3775fb9600/raw",
